<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southern Netherlands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> were the provinces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> that remained under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>, corresponding roughly to modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> and Luxembourg. Ruled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> until 1714 and then by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, they were also called the Spanish and Austrian Netherlands. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-republic">Dutch Republic</a> garrisoned barrier fortresses there after 1715, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> annexed the region in 1795.</p></div>
